  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "875abb31",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Drop redundant columns, encode categoricals + target\n",
    "\n",
    "- `fnlwgt` is a census sampling weight, not a property of the person, so it is dropped.\n",
    "- `education` duplicates the ordinal `education-num`, so it is dropped.\n",
    "- Nominal categoricals are one-hot encoded (a `LabelEncoder` would impose a fake ordering that hurts\n",
    "  Logistic Regression, KNN, SVC and Naive Bayes). The `OneHotEncoder` is fit on train only and ignores\n",
    "  categories unseen at test time, so train and test share exactly the same columns."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "id": "87f3c383",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-20T12:35:57.533927Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-09-20T12:35:57.533846Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-09-20T12:35:57.594354Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-09-20T12:35:57.592902Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "categorical: ['workclass', 'marital-status', 'occupation', 'relationship', 'race', 'sex', 'native-country']\n",
      "numeric: ['age', 'education-num', 'capital-gain', 'capital-loss', 'hours-per-week']\n",
      "target classes: {'<=50K': np.int64(0), '>50K': np.int64(1)}\n",
      "one-hot columns: 82\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "target_col = 'income'\n",
    "DROP_COLS = ['fnlwgt', 'education']\n",
    "train_df = train_df.drop(columns=DROP_COLS)\n",
    "test_df = test_df.drop(columns=DROP_COLS)\n",
    "\n",
    "cat_cols = train_df.select_dtypes(exclude='number').columns.drop(target_col).tolist()\n",
    "num_cols = [c for c in train_df.columns if c not in cat_cols + [target_col]]\n",
    "print('categorical:', cat_cols)\n",
    "print('numeric:', num_cols)\n",
    "\n",
    "target_le = LabelEncoder()\n",
    "y_train = pd.Series(target_le.fit_transform(train_df[target_col]), name=target_col)\n",
    "y_test = pd.Series(target_le.transform(test_df[target_col]), name=target_col)\n",
    "print('target classes:', dict(zip(target_le.classes_, target_le.transform(target_le.classes_))))\n",
    "\n",
    "ohe = OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown='ignore', sparse_output=False)\n",
    "X_train_cat = pd.DataFrame(ohe.fit_transform(train_df[cat_cols]), columns=ohe.get_feature_names_out(cat_cols))\n",
    "X_test_cat = pd.DataFrame(ohe.transform(test_df[cat_cols]), columns=ohe.get_feature_names_out(cat_cols))\n",
    "print('one-hot columns:', X_train_cat.shape[1])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "dbb906d2",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Feature/target split + scaling\n",
    "\n",
    "Numeric columns are standardized with a `StandardScaler` fit on train only (needed by KNN, SVC, MLP and\n",
    "Logistic Regression); the one-hot columns stay 0/1."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "id": "5115c53a",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-20T12:35:57.595832Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-09-20T12:35:57.595728Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-09-20T12:35:57.616611Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-09-20T12:35:57.616185Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "X_train: (30139, 87)  X_test: (15060, 87)\n",
      "columns match: True\n",
      "NaNs: 0 0\n",
      "class balance (train):\n",
      "income\n",
      "0    0.751\n",
      "1    0.249\n",
      "Name: proportion, dtype: float64\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "scaler = StandardScaler()\n",
    "X_train_num = pd.DataFrame(scaler.fit_transform(train_df[num_cols]), columns=num_cols)\n",
    "X_test_num = pd.DataFrame(scaler.transform(test_df[num_cols]), columns=num_cols)\n",
    "\n",
    "X_train_scaled = pd.concat([X_train_num, X_train_cat], axis=1)\n",
    "X_test_scaled = pd.concat([X_test_num, X_test_cat], axis=1)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('X_train:', X_train_scaled.shape, ' X_test:', X_test_scaled.shape)\n",
    "print('columns match:', list(X_train_scaled.columns) == list(X_test_scaled.columns))\n",
    "print('NaNs:', int(X_train_scaled.isna().sum().sum()), int(X_test_scaled.isna().sum().sum()))\n",
    "print('class balance (train):')\n",
    "print(y_train.value_counts(normalize=True).round(4))"
   ]
  },
  {
